{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc","id":487412,"title":"eventual new Aberrant-super strength etc.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-21T10:24:15-07:00","id":487412,"title":"eventual new Aberrant-super strength etc.","content":"With the OPP folks keeping rather hush hush on the sardonyx rulesystem, and the knowledge that it be core-trinity continuum (aeon time first)- then Aberrant, we have a bit of time to sit on our hands or play the old system. Question to you folks, is this: most people have issues with mega strength and the amount of auto successes it gives based on number of dots. I love it, yet still gripe when a player says they hit my npc bad guy for 20 auto and 12 dice and his soak is 9. &quot;Great...new npc needed.&quot; The auto dice lets me know &quot;that person is STRONG!&quot; and it makes sense when thinking about how a superman or a colossus could paste a random thug, but to keep headaches down, how have you ran Aberrant differently to adjust for the strongest wins all issue (in regards to the power creep of m. Strength vs soak abilities)? Keep lifting the same but reduced auto for damage? Make the player focus on one or the other? Adjusted soak to be more powerful (adding say, quantum lvl to all soak ratings?) One gm in my group reduces the auto dam/successes from 5 per dot to 2/3/2/3/2 going from 1-5 mega str. Another just hands out better body armor to all npc's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T10:27:33-07:00","id":487423,"title":"","content":"I pose the question simply to keep my mind off the fact that I dont know how the new system will work, and that I dont have my hands on it yet. Since some of my group hate not having perfect balance, im looking for ways to adjust our current games until we can finally be blessed with the new system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T14:28:30-07:00","id":487632,"title":"","content":"I suppose it's worth asking what the balance is meant to be between - ST and PC? Easy, you are both playing from the same rule-book. Purchase Invulnerability twice to sneak around the 'can't possess both Invunerability: Physical and Invulnerability: Energy' - if the players can do the math and question why you can do this and they can't simply point out to them that it's merely a stop-gap and beyond 6-7 Quantum their Mega-Strength successes will be ruling the day again.<br /> Then; simply never give out enough xp. or stack every other soaking mechanism until parity is reached. This isn't elegant and more or less ends up as a kind of arms war that the PCs can never win - but that's how i've seen Aberrant end up a few times now.<br /> Balance between Nova PC and baseline NPC? Quit your fussing, Novas are meant to feel unchallenged by baselines. The first ever Action Comics Superman story features Supes owning on a car with two armed gangsters inside. Eventually, Aberrant war needs for human survival in battle spawned VARGS (mechanized armour suits) and orbital weapon deployment standards but i doubt those measures saved many lives when a nova-bastard went in for sheer kills.<br /> There is another thread on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/420749-novas-vs-psions-balance-and-setting\">Balance between Novas and Psions</a> where i've posted at length about my own experiences with 2120 'balances'.<br /> If i'm misunderstanding you, let me know and i'll try to expand/clarify/reinterpret...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T15:50:22-07:00","id":487754,"title":"","content":"Oh no, you are mostly spot on. I dont mind the mega strength issue, its more with our 2nd Aberrant gm that hates how many successes you get (he has weakened it like I stated previously 2/3/2/3/2) and has limited how many dots we can buy. Mind you, im the only one that runs all three eras (adventure, aberrant, and trinity) and I allow all three to run together and I make sure that whoever decides to play a nova needs to know that they shouldnt feel bad for possibly pasting a heroic inspired.<br /> Balance in this instance would be &quot;what are some ways to adjust or play super strength, so that the other pc's arent watching their tounges around the guy who can putty them in 3 seconds&quot; one gm limits rhe ability outright. Another simply gives away &quot;advanced body armor&quot; like oprah giving out cars. I just tell them that A: always a bigger fish, and B: thats a lot of strength...but how strong is your willpower roll? <br /> And really, as previously stated, im just trying to keep aberrant/adventure/trinity talk going till continuum is ready...keepin me sane and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T15:53:47-07:00","id":487757,"title":"","content":"Since it was mentioned IIRC, theat they are doing away with mega dice, along with epic in Scion, I was wondering what are the ways you guys and gals might go about it? Would super strength be a power? Super speed already is, why not strength? (Id say because its a stat already...but this is why im not a game designer...among many other reasons.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T19:16:46-07:00","id":487849,"title":"","content":"So in relation to player vs player you mean, or at least Adventure! creations versus Aberrant generated Novas - if i'm understanding.<br /> The best approach, fundamentally, is evasion and range. Adventure! works well with Trinity, but my brother had the most experience using Adventure! in an Aberrant game. I seem to remember he used a variant of 'Untouchable' (Adventure! p162) for an NPC martial artist Daredevil to stay alive in a few battles against a 20-50xp nova with combat powers. But i can't recall any details on how precisely that worked. One could imagine another equivilent Knack might make 'splash damage' effects easier to avoid when the damage breaks line of sight - via sundered objects and scenery rent apart by Mega-Strength attacks.<br /> Depending on how you run Dramatic Editing, that could also play a role, so could super science.<br /> -shrug-<br /> I might even be tempted to use the destruction facet as a type of foil to Mega-Strength - somehow able to redirect the destructive force of the given nova into scenery and other unintended targets. But in my imagining, the higher echelons on Destructive inspired should have some way to play a role in mega-strength battles - simply by right of the mastered facet.<br /> To really cross them over with PC parity, you may need to introduce some ST-only Knacks to balance out in-game before offering them to players.<br /> I have to admit that i've little experience with Adventure! systems, but the idea wouldn't be giving those characters greater power, but in extending some counter-balance to the extremes presented in so many automatic successes.<br /> It's an interesting question, as with many problems Mega-Strength presents, i would have to think about it.<br /> <br /> The way i've tried to limit this in my most recent games was with Noetic/Subquantum jargon - the drive being; the Subquantum medium of 2100+ is soaked in too much Psi for higher Quantum novas to erupt - using the Asia Ascendant rules for those that erupt at lower power. During the 1998-2060 period, the appropriately thick Quantum miasma for true Novas at full strength to erupt exists, the side effect of that extreme being taint. But the naturally occuring Psiads become rarer than normal - although we're given no reason to believe Daredevil/Talent inspired are affected by the Psi/Quantum medium. Then getting back to the days of Adventure!, you see the balanced Hammersmith Event which generated the lower intensity inspired but doesn't have the 'taint' to generate actual Aberrant-book Novas. Only the prime Stalwart; Primoris compares, but it takes him close to a century to get the level we see Mal at.<br /> All that just to say; 'play the appropriate inspiration type, please'.<br /> -smile-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T19:41:11-07:00","id":487861,"title":"","content":"If it were me, I would boost the effectiveness of soak just a hair, and maybe include some inherent soaking abilities, say, based off Quantum. Strength should still be ahead - offense trumping defense is good for your game, ultimately - but not that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:38:45-07:00","id":488871,"title":"","content":"This goes to a debate a friend of mine and I had. He believed that Damage = Soak. I believe that Damage &gt; Soak or else combats get so bogged down. Additionally Soak &gt; Skill. In other words, the person who can tank anything should not be on the same par as someone who just dodges or parries everything away. Mr. Soak can just take it all day long and then laugh at the little guy acting like Daffy Duck on speed. Lastly Skill &gt; Damage. Meaning the guy who can hop all around should be able to not worry about Mr. Smashieface. That is how I balance out those three parts of combat.<br /> There should always be balance on some level, even if in the all-dreaded white room scenario. I hate those but they do happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:30:00-07:00","id":488909,"title":"","content":"Right. Generally, if defense outstrips offense, combat gets really...really...sloooow. You have to whittle down all of your opponents bit by bit, and that gets boring, quickly.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, damage offense outstrips damage too much, you can't really have an exciting battle, because it's basically over before it starts. That's the current Aberrant problem. Poking the bad guy in the chest and having him instantly explode is funny a few times, but gets old. Likewise a player basically just getting one-shotted is not fun.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm not sure their needs to be a big difference between Skill and Soak based defenses - honestly, that just seems like a matter of preferred style to anything else. Really they should probably be equally effective, or you start seeing people shift to one or the other just for the advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T07:50:08-07:00","id":489480,"title":"","content":"I totally agree with you on the fact that Damage should not go too too far out. Then it does get just as boring. <br /> &quot;Yawn. Roll your to-hit roll. Ok. You hit. He is now a fine red mist. Next guy is over there.&quot;<br /> I have been in those fights and the answer is not to just go with the &quot;bigger fish&quot; route but to have to nerf the rules. It has been my experience as a player that when the ST comes up with someone bigger and nastier than you, then I only see two words flash in my head: Challenge Accepted. I then work on trying to beat that guy. Most players I know are of similar bent, however your mileage may vary. <br /> I choose to opt to rework the rules. Perhaps my mention of nerfing was a bit harsh but, when you retool the rules to make things fair overall, most players think you are picking on them specifically and will ask why you are weakening them. Again, I say most and your table and players may think differently. I do know that the rules are made to keep things fair for everyone. I do know that the rules are even playtested to make sure that this happens. However, no committee can ever hope to compete with the multitudes and their ability to come up with new and interesting twists to things. Twists that make one particular character an unstoppable monster. So, I am always a fan of house rules to keep things easy and fair for everyone at the table.<br /> As far as the difference between Skill and Soak goes, I can see how you may think they are just flavors of defense. I also will not insult your intelligence by explaining the differences between them. You are experienced enough to know what I mean. But I see them as not just styles but actual choices to make. Soak is very static. It just is something that you can reach. Skill is something that can be changed and it can be altered over time. It is a bit more dynamic on things, IMO. There is also the fact that, when someone focuses on a skill, then they tend to have less defenses and less offense, Instead, opting to just not being hit and not taking any damage at all if they have any say about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T15:41:27-07:00","id":489920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=489480#post489480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I choose to opt to rework the rules. Perhaps my mention of nerfing was a bit harsh but, when you retool the rules to make things fair overall, most players think you are picking on them specifically and will ask why you are weakening them. Again, I say most and your table and players may think differently. I do know that the rules are made to keep things fair for everyone. I do know that the rules are even playtested to make sure that this happens. However, no committee can ever hope to compete with the multitudes and their ability to come up with new and interesting twists to things. Twists that make one particular character an unstoppable monster. So, I am always a fan of house rules to keep things easy and fair for everyone at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with house-ruling if need be, although my preference is that I shouldn't have to houserule immediately obvious combinations. Also I think it's better to boost than to nerf if it can be helped at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as the difference between Skill and Soak goes, I can see how you may think they are just flavors of defense. I also will not insult your intelligence by explaining the differences between them. You are experienced enough to know what I mean. But I see them as not just styles but actual choices to make. Soak is very static. It just is something that you can reach. Skill is something that can be changed and it can be altered over time. It is a bit more dynamic on things, IMO. There is also the fact that, when someone focuses on a skill, then they tend to have less defenses and less offense, Instead, opting to just not being hit and not taking any damage at all if they have any say about it. </div> </div> </div>Skill should certainly be more variable, as whether my reactions are up to snuff any given day has a lot of ongoing factors, but my overall toughness isn't really going to vary all that much, minute to minute.<br /> <br /> I do think that a skill based defense (dodging, blocking, parrying, what-have-you) should be part and parcel of your attack skill really, because nobody teaches you how to attack WITHOUT teaching you how to get out of the way/take a blow., but that opinion seems fairly controversial at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T21:58:34-07:00","id":490192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc#post487412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the OPP folks keeping rather hush hush on the sardonyx rulesystem, and the knowledge that it be core-trinity continuum (aeon time first)- then Aberrant, we have a bit of time to sit on our hands or play the old system. Question to you folks, is this: most people have issues with mega strength and the amount of auto successes it gives based on number of dots. I love it, yet still gripe when a player says they hit my npc bad guy for 20 auto and 12 dice and his soak is 9. &quot;Great...new npc needed.&quot; . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you tried calling your players out, ethically? Good guys generally don't go around slaughtering every thug/jerk/bad guy they see . . .<br /> <br /> There's a brief monologue from the <b>Justice League</b> animated series that drives this home. At the end, when Superman is battling Darkseid. And Superman begins talking about how he has to be so careful in battle, even against the most evil foes. That living with superstrength is like walking through a movie set, where everything is made of cardboard and Styrofoam, and it would be so easy to accidentally crush someone . . . And how battling Darkseid, for the first time in his life, he doesn't have to hold back. For once, he can lay into a bad guy as much as he wants (and the bad guy deserves), and not worry about the consequences. He can lash out with everything he has, pouring all of his anger and frustration into his punches, because Darkseid can take it (and not instantly die).<br /> <br /> So if you're running a &quot;good guy&quot; campaign, and the PCs are just beating the thugs to death, make them own the consequences. Turn the press against them, with shocking exposes and editorials on the monstrous, murderous PCs. Let them watch their toy sales plummet, and have their sponsors drop them. Have their friends shun them, and kick 'em out of the Amp Club. Bring in the cops, and arrest 'em for murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 04-24-2015, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T10:12:05-07:00","id":490657,"title":"","content":"The World of Cardboard speech: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cl_5UwS57X8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cl_5UwS57X8</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T16:15:05-07:00","id":491043,"title":"","content":"Thats one of my absolute favorite JL moments. (Supes is my fav DC character) well, most often, the players that splatter random goons or even big bads with not super soaks, take that as the moment they shift their characters from &quot;I wont kill. Its my one rule.&quot; To &quot;some bad guys need to die...cause they are bad.&quot; And for the life of me, my group cant seem to stop doing that. Everyone likes being the boyscout...until they screw up, then its &quot;well...time to get my wolverine on. He is cooler anyway.&quot; One gm has started to pressure the group in game when someone kills someone with &quot;you realize you are a murderer now?&quot; And I like that. But some still hold to &quot;greater good&quot; and smashy away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T07:57:23-07:00","id":491655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=490192#post490192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you tried calling your players out, ethically? Good guys generally don't go around slaughtering every thug/jerk/bad guy they see . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really about PCs being too murder happy, or going around popping thugs like pimples. Moral consequences are an unrelated problem.<br /> <br /> No, the problem is when it IS Darkseid, and he just gets splattered in an instant because offense so badly outstrips defense. Then you have a whole revolving door of these guys, and it breaks suspension of disbelief. The only narrative solution (that is, fixing the problem via story rather than house-ruling) is to have your bad guy operate from behind the shadows so the PCs have to do a lot of leg work to find the bastard, and then when they do find him you get to give the poor slob all of 30 seconds of actual characterization before the PCs whomp him. That's no fun as ST.<br /> <br /> Likewise, even if the PCs aren't killing everyone in one turn, but knocking out everyone in one turn, it's the same problem. The fight is over before the bell rings.<br /> <br /> Also, this is a system that has to serve Scion, and Scion will include things you will want to/have to kill because there is no way for the mortal populace to deal with it otherwise.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> I might make the argument that Aberrant really isn't, or at least wasn't, the game for &quot;good guys&quot;. The setting presented was much darker than most classical superhero settings, and the overall focus seemed to be less superheros as moral police - a large number of novas are mercenaries, for example, and mercenaries engaged in a third world conflict killing people isn't particularly news worthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T11:24:02-07:00","id":491799,"title":"","content":"Well, Aberrant definitely should have lethal superpowers, IMO. If you're strong enough, and they aren't tough enough, you'll just punch a hole through them. That's kind of one of things I like about Aberrant, you don't just win because you're the hero, you only win if you have the smarts, the guts and, critically, the <i>power</i> to win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T13:04:46-07:00","id":491876,"title":"","content":"I have no problem if the character played is a darker toned merc type. Its just that the group doesnt make them that way, they just &quot;flip a switch one day&quot; and convert. Solar-totally true. Aberrant should have lethal powers. Im completely ok with it...the question I have is how have other gm's adjusted so that their bad guys dont have to all be soak machines AND super willpower strong AND smart enough to screw with the pcs to survive a single punch/single domination/mental blast and be not game breaking every dot filled sheets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T15:21:22-07:00","id":492018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=491876#post491876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the question I have is how have other gm's adjusted so that their bad guys dont have to all be soak machines AND super willpower strong AND smart enough to screw with the pcs to survive a single punch/single domination/mental blast and be not game breaking every dot filled sheets.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, thinking of enemies as 'bad guys' doesn't help you out - the idea is to make everyone sympathetic. The world of cardboard bit is only as effective due to Supes' universally understood restraint against 'bad guys' - showing a level of care and regard for life in the character's approach to his power even against most of his worst enemies who have threatened mass murder countless times prior. It would sound stupid coming from a Lobo or any other anti-hero who didn't give a toss.<br /> <br /> I'll throw out a few ideas for narrative aversion of mega-combat and you can take what you please, if any pleases you at all:<br /> I saw some success with a combination of a couple of bodiless characters (one via tainted permanent density decrease, another via neural upload), the social combat system in Forceful Personalities (plus some mental attempts), subquantum jargon, public pressure and endless hordes of squishy, human guilt-trips (usually behind the controls of a main battle tank, fighter jet or attack helicopter).<br /> It seems like a nice anti-PC could help you, a character with whom the player is inexorably destined to clash with, but is measurably more noble than they and won't lower themself to the PCs level. Mix up the perception of good and evil, redeem 'evil' npcs the PCs have vanquished and sully pure npcs after following a PCs poor advice/lead. With all due respect, if the PCs treat a turned friend no differently than the average foe, then there may be a problem with characterization on one side of the screen or the other.<br /> A good recurring boss for Aberrants is one the PCs a strong stake in not killing - their actual boss; who pays their checks, gives them equipment and lends them some influence when required might escape summary execution after a few schemes to embarrass or otherwise one-up the players, same with any established characters who the players have invested in - by whatever means.<br /> While we're on the subject, fans, admirers and saved baselines tend to massage the PC ego enough to slip them under their skin with a little targeted characterization. Funny characters can also win points with player perceptions - the idea is to make them want to be better via emotional manipulation by proxy of actors. Make the PCs social standing matter, make it a real thing that touches them in game so that they don't want to go without it.<br /> Make a character arc out of the Nova's capacity for destruction - i've enabled more than one murderous PC into remorseful acts and more with a personally crafted subplot just for them. Do it right and they won't even know you did it, but be cautious to not drag players in directions they don't want any part of - that's no fun. I've found a few players who were frightfully immune to NPC or setting manipulations (often also equally prone to murder) - and you may need a nice tasty carrot and a stick to keep them civilized for long.<br /> Do stories that make enemies weilding ungodly levels of anti-nova tech commonplace - handwave and force every last drop of quantum you can from characters prior to a named villain encounter and distract them heavily both during and afterwards. Always plan a couple of escapes (at least) for climactic encounters you could be interested in extending.<br /> Never leave a character hanging without a deadline - the PCs will find a way given the opportunity, so keep them off balance and divide their attention. This can be frustrating when you want to characterize the NPC you are protecting - but given enough lucky/daring escapes, the players will start going out of their way to draw you out on the details they missed earlier, in preparation for their next chance to dick-punch them.<br /> <br /> But in the end, i'm perhaps not the best advisor - in my experience, Aberrant eventually always breaks down into an arms race between players and ST. Every pool is ten or higher and certain powers are required for any characters wishing to be competitive in X or Y. While i don't at all disagree with Solar, i've found Aberrant power begins getting in the way of more local/personal storytelling scales. Which just seems a strange tangent for such a character driven setting to be derailed onto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Oops... 04-25-2015, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T20:44:01-07:00","id":492250,"title":"","content":"I appreciate what you are trying to say here, Nihilist, but you really are wandering off on a tangent. I'm saying I can't take my friends to lunch because my car won't start. You are saying my friends just need to eat less. That may be true <i>but that is not the problem I'm concerned about</i>.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T21:05:07-07:00","id":492275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=492250#post492250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate what you are trying to say here, Nihilist, but you really are wandering off on a tangent. I'm saying I can't take my friends to lunch because my car won't start. You are saying my friends just need to eat less. That may be true <i>but that is not the problem I'm concerned about</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That statement is just so awesome, I simply <i>have </i>to make it into my signature quote. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Done!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 04-26-2015, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T11:54:40-07:00","id":492783,"title":"","content":"Okay, i can accept that.<br /> -blush-<br /> I apologize if i've spun tangential, i thought ManBearPig asked how other STs had avoided the cookie-cutter antagonist mill in the previous post. But, if what i've posted isn't helpful, then by all means point out my deviation. I'm just glad your response was worthy of praise by Su-tehp, otherwise the post would have been a total waste of my time.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> Metaphors provide scant context, but if by '<i>friends eating</i>' you mean Aberrant PCs engaging in challenging high-level physical conflict and if '<i>broken car</i>' means cheap systemic superiority of Mega-Strength to most (if not all) soak powers; then there are three paths immediately obvious to me:<br /> De-power Mega-Strength<br /> Empower soak (but not enough to outstrip damage in the endgame)<br /> Narrate your way out of the conundrum<br /> <br /> Since balance can remain iffy with the first two options, i decided to suggest the third.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> At risk of straying further tangent-wise and wasting more time, i'll try defining the issues by mechanism of extremes. In the process, i've found that Aberrant soak eventually outstrips physical damage but at much greater expense, which Wolfgar has already pointed out as a poor endgame experience. So, if anything - Mega-Strength is the one that needs more by the end - as there are many more sources of soak out there than of extra physical damage.<br /> <br /> Strength 5 + Mega 5 + Node 5 + Crush = 81-133xp or 18-20 nova points for +25B-45L auto damage and 5+ dice (+1 auto damage and all damage made lethal for 1q per turn; +20 auto damage and all damage made lethal for 20q per turn)<br /> <br /> Stamina 5 + Mega 5 + Resilience x 2 + Durability + Armor 5 = 127-167xp or 39-41 nova points for 35/25 soak (soak all as bashing for 1q per turn), 10 health levels<br /> <br /> Strength 5 + Mega 10 + Node 5 + Crush = 256-308xp or 33-35 nova points for +50B-70L auto damage and 5+ dice (+1 auto damage and all damage made lethal for 1q per turn; +20 auto damage and all damage made lethal for 20q per turn)<br /> <br /> Stamina 5 + Mega 10 + Resilience x 2 + Durability + Armor 5 + Invulnerability (All Physical Extra) 5 = 381-421xp or 79-81 nova points for 75/65 soak (soak all as bashing for 1q per turn), 20 health levels<br /> <br /> P.S. Didn't include Quantum costs, but that's not too hard to figure in. Pure oversight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Character math 04-26-2015, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T19:08:12-07:00","id":493131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=492783#post492783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, i can accept that.<br /> -blush-<br /> I apologize if I've spun tangential, i thought ManBearPig asked how other STs had avoided the cookie-cutter antagonist mill in the previous post. But, if what I've posted isn't helpful, then by all means point out my deviation. I'm just glad your response was worthy of praise by Su-tehp, otherwise the post would have been a total waste of my time.<br /> -smile-</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, all this stuff about Mega-Attributes is waaay beyond me. I'm far more familiar with the rules of Trinity than I am with Aberrant or Adventure, but even that's not saying much. And the story aspects of these roleplaying games I find far more fascinating than the rules and number-crunching.<br /> <br /> All the same, I know a good thing when I see it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 04-26-2015, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T21:49:28-07:00","id":493255,"title":"","content":"No need to be embarrassed. It's a forum; threads tend to wander.<br /> <br /> Those number though assume a person maxed out for defense, but that isn't going to fit everyone's concept, and would mean a huge drain on resources to remain viable. Your super scientists, psychics, and elemental controllers aren't going to have max Stamina, Mega-Stamina, and Armor; and that in turn makes them far squishier than they would be in almost any other game. Is that gonna be fun making them sit out everything, because the minute some actually starts a fight they get crushed?<br /> <br /> Also I might suggest <b>Claws</b> as part of the high end load-out; I usually think more in terms of &quot;Energy Fists&quot;. Maxed out it provides a +5 to damage, makes the damage lethal, is cheaper to use than Crush, and doesn't take an extra turn to use - you can even pop claws or ignite your fists in the same turn you start beating ass. It's a cheap five nova points, or 15 XP.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, even the monstrous defense load out doesn't stand a chance against a single level of Quantum Inferno, but that's really more for destroying planets anyway.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T21:52:44-07:00","id":493259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=493131#post493131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll admit, all this stuff about Mega-Attributes is waaay beyond me. I'm far more familiar with the rules of Trinity than I am with Aberrant or Adventure, but even that's not saying much. And the story aspects of these roleplaying games I find far more fascinating than the rules and number-crunching.<br /> <br /> All the same, I know a good thing when I see it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was a more notable problem/complication/feature in Aberrant and Scion. Trinity and Adventure had their own headaches, of course.<br /> <br /> The story aspect brings you to the table, but the rules aspect should serve that story, so it's in the best interest of people who know these things to make it that you never have that story disrupted due to weird math.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T23:36:42-07:00","id":493318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=493259#post493259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a more notable problem/complication/feature in Aberrant and Scion. Trinity and Adventure had their own headaches, of course.<br /> <br /> The story aspect brings you to the table, but the rules aspect should serve that story, so it's in the best interest of people who know these things to make it that you never have that story disrupted due to weird math.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1. Hell, the broken vehicle/spaceship combat rules in Trinity are giving me headaches now just because I can't figure out exactly how many Structural Levels each type of spaceship mentioned in Trinity needs to have. See here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/488990-trinity-starship-sheets-did-any-fan-make-these\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...fan-make-these</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T06:02:27-07:00","id":493515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=493255#post493255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those number though assume a person maxed out for defense, but that isn't going to fit everyone's concept, and would mean a huge drain on resources to remain viable. Your super scientists, psychics, and elemental controllers aren't going to have max Stamina, Mega-Stamina, and Armor; and that in turn makes them far squishier than they would be in almost any other game. Is that gonna be fun making them sit out everything, because the minute some actually starts a fight they get crushed?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that was solely for the illustration of Mega-Strength auto damage capping out prior to soak getting anywhere near a cap. I included the xp values to show exactly how distant some of these goals would actually be. Of course this isn't representative of 'average' novas - i'm purely concentrating on damage vs soak relating to Mega-Strength in it's native system. I think that's what the topic is about, right?<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I might suggest <b>Claws</b> as part of the high end load-out; I usually think more in terms of &quot;Energy Fists&quot;. Maxed out it provides a +5 to damage, makes the damage lethal, is cheaper to use than Crush, and doesn't take an extra turn to use - you can even pop claws or ignite your fists in the same turn you start beating ass. It's a cheap five nova points, or 15 XP. </div> </div> </div>I did consider that, but since it's the only power off the top of my head that added damage in a forest of powers that added soak - i chose to leave some mystery in.<br /> -shrug-<br /> It also adds dice and not auto damage, which is a little less difficult to manage and would just distract from the comparison more than i already have. But, i did figure this into my thinking...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Incidentally, even the monstrous defense load out doesn't stand a chance against a single level of Quantum Inferno, but that's really more for destroying planets anyway.) </div> </div> </div>That's probably a whole other thread...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=493259#post493259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The story aspect brings you to the table, but the rules aspect should serve that story, so it's in the best interest of people who know these things to make it that you never have that story disrupted due to weird math.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree - the rules should be lurking beneath the surface - you do not give PCs side-by-side comparisons of melee damage vs soak at character generation. That could scare some of them off in Aberrant.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=493318#post493318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+1. Hell, the broken vehicle/spaceship combat rules in Trinity are giving me headaches now just because I can't figure out exactly how many Structural Levels each type of spaceship mentioned in Trinity needs to have. See here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/488990-trinity-starship-sheets-did-any-fan-make-these\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...fan-make-these</a></div> </div> </div> </div>-sympathetic chuckle-<br /> I needed to rework them myself eventually - i can just give you my figures, but they are no more official than any values you side with. I think my numbers could have been entrenched in house-rules so deep they render them unusable however. Ultimately, it depends on what you want to balance for. PM me if you wish, i'll see if i can fish them out - or just arrive at the numbers again...<br /> -blush-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:48:55-07:00","id":493740,"title":"","content":"I like everything being said here, and honestly...the REAL point of my original post was simply to keep those of us who play the Adventure/Aberrant/Trinity games talking. My favorite games, and I get lonely when i sign on here and the last comment on this forum page is a week old. True, more recently, folks have been talking about Divis or Mercer...but before that, there was a time where id check and go all frowny face cause no one was saying anything. So ya know...yay for convo <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T15:13:32-07:00","id":493978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=493740#post493740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like everything being said here, and honestly...the REAL point of my original post was simply to keep those of us who play the Adventure/Aberrant/Trinity games talking. My favorite games, and I get lonely when i sign on here and the last comment on this forum page is a week old. True, more recently, folks have been talking about Divis or Mercer...but before that, there was a time where id check and go all frowny face cause no one was saying anything. So ya know...yay for convo <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've always liked the Aeonverse, though (as I've mentioned before repeatedly so forgive the broken record effect I'm having here) I've always been far more partial to Trinity than to Aberrant or to Adventure. I love the sci-fi of Trinity, I like the geopolitical intrigue of Aberrant, but I'm admittedly meh about the pulp fiction of Adventure. Even so, the entire Aeonverse metaplot does appeal to me as a whole; it's an epic of great potential. I managed to get copies of almost all the books as they came out, which was great because (if I understand correctly) these books are now only available as PDF files and are not Print On Demand.<br /> <br /> But I didn't find out until perhaps a few months ago that the Trinity Continuum was being rebooted and recreated with new books. Needless to say, I squee'd. I freely admit that. Hell, the only reason I'm on this forum now after nearly a year's absence is because I got burned out on playing World of Warcraft and needed a break from raiding. The whim arose to visit this forum and see what was going on...and the rest is history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T15:32:42-07:00","id":493982,"title":"","content":"I've liked it, and always had a soft spot for the setting. Aeon was really cool and versatile, Adventure was really well done, and Aberrant is honestly my favorite superhero system, mostly because it bolts together a system I'm comfortable with without bogging things down too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T20:22:57-07:00","id":494295,"title":"","content":"i dont think strength is the problem people think it is. the reason mega-strength is so potent, is that it has to be in order to keep up with an equal investment in quantum bolt+quantum, which does the damage of an artillery strike at the high end. balance is about comparing alternatives for same cost.<br /> <br /> and on the defense side, for an equal investment you could get enough soak to withstand the average attack- and still die in one hit to a very high roll. but then a high-rolling force field could survive even that with the right dice pool.<br /> <br /> i think we need a new mega-stamina enhancement- spend 1 quantum point, and that lethal hit simply incapacitates you, just short of death. then some mechanism of how long your out based on how excessive the damage was. it would be very theme-appropriate, useful for keeping important characters alive, and also leave the character helpless for some time. this would fit well with some of the other things novas can do anyway, and not make anyone better at winning a fight. does make murdering someone more difficult, but not impossible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4695-teulisch","name":"Teulisch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T21:07:12-07:00","id":494339,"title":"","content":"Everyone posting here is clearly invested in the setting - in the years post-cancellation many of us took the system under-wing and used it as our own. Because there aren't throngs of us, there are times the forum cools down for days - like a bad run of rolls. But after a decade of waiting, we've all become pretty patient too.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teulisch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=494295#post494295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i dont think strength is the problem people think it is. the reason mega-strength is so potent, is that it has to be in order to keep up with an equal investment in quantum bolt+quantum, which does the damage of an artillery strike at the high end. balance is about comparing alternatives for same cost.<br /> <br /> and on the defense side, for an equal investment you could get enough soak to withstand the average attack- and still die in one hit to a very high roll. but then a high-rolling force field could survive even that with the right dice pool.<br /> <br /> i think we need a new mega-stamina enhancement- spend 1 quantum point, and that lethal hit simply incapacitates you, just short of death. then some mechanism of how long your out based on how excessive the damage was. it would be very theme-appropriate, useful for keeping important characters alive, and also leave the character helpless for some time. this would fit well with some of the other things novas can do anyway, and not make anyone better at winning a fight. does make murdering someone more difficult, but not impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point that M-Strength is balanced against Q-bolt, the cost is much more comparable there. I left out any rolling defences in the numbers above because of the variables i would then need to account for - but it was there in the back of my mind.<br /> I'd like to see some kind of safe-guard against casual, accidental murder at higher levels - if it happens all the time it loses its impact as a dramatic hook. A simple M-Stamina enhancement could fill that need. Good idea. Want to expand on how it would work, since it's your concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:33:10-07:00","id":494780,"title":"","content":"yeah, I can think of a few ways to make it better....<br /> <br /> <b>Unkillable</b> (mega-stamina enhancement)<br /> <br /> if an attack does damage that would kill you, this enhancement spends one quantum point to prevent you from dropping below incapacitated either for the scene, or until you are healed above incapacitated. while in this state, you appear dead to outside observers, but your node is still active and node activity may still be observed. you will remain in this state until you can heal to crippled on your own (see p. 254), or are healed by someone else. if you take damage again during this time that would kill you, this enhancement will spend one quantum point to keep you alive for the scene. you cannot regain quantum pool while incapacitated in this manner. this enhancement is passive, and will not function if you are dormned down. no other powers may be activated while incapacitated. if you spend your last quantum to stay alive, you may require medical help to survive. each time you are attacked such that this enhancement must spend quantum to keep you alive, the time to heal starts over. each time this enhancement activates, gain one temporary taint.<br /> once a nova will this enhancement heals to crippled, he may start gaining quantum pool again and will appear alive again, but will not awaken until healed to maimed, although regeneration may be used once quantum pool is full. injuries that require the use of this power will leave scars, which may be healed with regeneration.<br /> <br /> special note- aggravated damage will only be survived if you have a way to soak agg damage, and this enhancement will automatically activate the appropriate enhancement or power if needed. healing from aggravated damage will take the full 5 months. if you cannot soak agg, then you are simply dead, and your body destroyed.<br /> <br /> so, this keeps you alive, and you have at least 3x healing rate from mega-stamina. you will likely be out of the action for a couple of months. The survival hibernation of this enhancement is similar to chrysalis in many ways. while it makes you difficult to kill, you may still die if they keep hitting your corpse, even if it takes a couple days of effort to do it. yes, this enhancement can survive a direct hit with a nuclear warhead, but you will need adaptability to survive the radiation that follows. as taint gain from repeated attacks can result in new aberrations, this may be a large clue to others that you are not dead. such aberrations will likely be quantum related.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4695-teulisch","name":"Teulisch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:04:47-07:00","id":495024,"title":"","content":"Did anyone else feel that a nova without Mega-Stamina was a wimp and oh-so-squishy? It is why I gave every player a Mega-Stamina of 1 with the Hardbody Enhancement and then I also gave them all Mega-Perception 1 with the Quantum Attunement Enhancement. Just because I liked the ideas of novas going &quot;My quantum sense is tingling&quot; or else &quot;I sense a disturbance in the quantum&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:40:39-07:00","id":495055,"title":"","content":"Unkillable sounds very similar to Superman's coma from &quot;The Death of Superman&quot; circa 92...I like it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:50:26-07:00","id":495064,"title":"","content":"As to how much I love the system, I have physical and pdf copies of the entire series, including fanmade, Adventure to Trinity. I love the line, the metaplot (even though I rarely use it) the ease of system use, and the feel of each era. Ive just simply run them all so many times rhat I have to change, edit, and adapt them to my own ideas. Combine trinity and Adventure-Firefly. Aberrant with less paranoia-DC Universe. With more infighting-Marvel. Adventure in modernish time-Watchmen. Trinity withless biokenisis-Star Wars <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T16:01:18-07:00","id":495344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teulisch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=494295#post494295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think strength is the problem people think it is. The reason mega-strength is so potent, is that it has to be in order to keep up with an equal investment in quantum bolt+quantum which does the damage of an artillery strike at the high end. Balance is about comparing alternatives for same cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Balance is about a lot of things...and may not even exist, but really this cuts to the heart of the issue that offense not only outstrips defense, but outstrips it by a wide margin. That's really the problem. It's not even that offense being better than defense is bad, because it keeps fights from turning into grindfests, but it does mean players have to put in effort they rather might not to keep up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T16:07:30-07:00","id":495348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teulisch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/487412-eventual-new-aberrant-super-strength-etc?p=494780#post494780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, I can think of a few ways to make it better....<br /> <br /> <b>Unkillable</b> (mega-stamina enhancement)<br /> <br /> if an attack does damage that would kill you, this enhancement spends one quantum point to prevent you from dropping below incapacitated either for the scene, or until you are healed above incapacitated. while in this state, you appear dead to outside observers, but your node is still active and node activity may still be observed. you will remain in this state until you can heal to crippled on your own (see p. 254), or are healed by someone else. if you take damage again during this time that would kill you, this enhancement will spend one quantum point to keep you alive for the scene. you cannot regain quantum pool while incapacitated in this manner. this enhancement is passive, and will not function if you are dormned down. no other powers may be activated while incapacitated. if you spend your last quantum to stay alive, you may require medical help to survive. each time you are attacked such that this enhancement must spend quantum to keep you alive, the time to heal starts over. each time this enhancement activates, gain one temporary taint.<br /> once a nova will this enhancement heals to crippled, he may start gaining quantum pool again and will appear alive again, but will not awaken until healed to maimed, although regeneration may be used once quantum pool is full. injuries that require the use of this power will leave scars, which may be healed with regeneration.<br /> <br /> special note- aggravated damage will only be survived if you have a way to soak agg damage, and this enhancement will automatically activate the appropriate enhancement or power if needed. healing from aggravated damage will take the full 5 months. if you cannot soak agg, then you are simply dead, and your body destroyed.<br /> <br /> so, this keeps you alive, and you have at least 3x healing rate from mega-stamina. you will likely be out of the action for a couple of months. The survival hibernation of this enhancement is similar to chrysalis in many ways. while it makes you difficult to kill, you may still die if they keep hitting your corpse, even if it takes a couple days of effort to do it. yes, this enhancement can survive a direct hit with a nuclear warhead, but you will need adaptability to survive the radiation that follows. as taint gain from repeated attacks can result in new aberrations, this may be a large clue to others that you are not dead. such aberrations will likely be quantum related.</div> </div> </div> </div>New Aberrations could also be sort of a &quot;Lazarus Pool&quot; effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T16:11:38-07:00","id":495352,"title":"","content":"The word balance is thrown about a lot. With Aberrant, things were lop-sided as all get out. However, bear in mind that balance should not be white-room balance. For example, it has been noted in this thread that the setting also helps to balance out the outlandish use of Mega-Str to rip people apart and then use their femurs as drumsticks. (Insert Nathan Explosion meme here) When you have someone turning people into smears and it gets out, then the universe tends to start putting obstacles in your way that have nothing to do with normal powers.<br /> In combat, everyone has their own strengths and weaknesses. Some things are OBVIOUS such as those who go Mega-Strength 5 and then enhancing it and adding to it as much as possible. Others are the people who get a ton of Mega-Social and enhancements. They can wreck a setting fast in practice. The math bears out that defense can easily be obliterated but it all depends on how you attack and defend. Density Decrease + Mega- Socials = Charming Ghost who makes you hit yourself until you die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T16:35:47-07:00","id":495376,"title":"","content":"Much of Aberrants balance was sort of a Rock Paper Scissors balance, which works. I just want to makes sure it's not Rock crushes Scissors, Rock crushes Paper more slowly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T17:12:20-07:00","id":495446,"title":"","content":"It does work and you are right about rock crushing all, but I would like it more akin to rock paper scissors lizard spock with a bit of variety in the way things are handled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:07:38-07:00","id":495621,"title":"","content":"RPSLS would also be acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}